2025-12-01 09:33:21,685 - benchmark.runner - INFO - Short answer: This week, Point Reyes National Seashore is your most reliable pick from San Francisco for good weather, minimal closures, short drive, and strong visitor services. A close second is Pinnacles National Park if you want dramatic rocks/caves and you can arrive early to avoid parking capacity limits.

Why (with numbers and sources)

Point Reyes National Seashore (code: pore)
- Distance from SF: about 30 miles north (NPS) — “Approximately 30 miles (50 km) north of San Francisco.” Source: NPS Point Reyes overview https://www.nps.gov/pore/index.htm
- Hours: Open daily 6:00 am–midnight (NPS). Source: same as above
- Visitor center: Bear Valley Visitor Center, daily 9:30–5:00 (closed Dec 25; usually closes 2 pm on Thanksgiving). Source: NPS Visitor Centers https://www.nps.gov/pore/planyourvisit/visitorcenters.htm#bearvalleyvc
- Entrance fee: None (NPS lists no fees). Source: park page above
- Active alerts: None (NPS alert feed returned 0). Source: NPS Alerts API result for pore
- Weather (Point Reyes Station): current ~45°F, overcast; 3‑day forecast highs 58–67°F, lows ~39–41°F, no precip indicated in forecast data returned.
  - 12/1: max 63.0°F / min 39.4°F (partly cloudy)
  - 12/2: max 58.3°F / min 40.1°F (partly cloudy)
  - 12/3: max 66.9°F / min 40.6°F (sunny)
  - Source: WeatherAPI via tool for Point Reyes Station, last updated 2025‑12‑01 01:15 local
- Bottom line: Closest national-park unit with mild coastal weather, no closures, no entrance fee, and an open visitor center for up-to-date conditions.

Pinnacles National Park (code: pinn) — best inland alternative
- Distance from SF: straight‑line ≈112 miles (computed from NPS coordinates: SF 37.78, -122.42; Pinnacles 36.4903, -121.1814). Note: driving distance is longer via US‑101/CA‑146 (west) or CA‑25 (east); there’s no through road between entrances. Source: NPS Pinnacles page https://www.nps.gov/pinn/index.htm
- Fee: $30/vehicle (valid 1–7 days). Source: NPS fees (same page)
- Hours: East entrance 24/7 year‑round; West entrance 7:30 am–8:00 pm. Source: NPS (same page)
- Visitor center: Bear Gulch Nature Center (east side) open 9:00–4:00 Mon/Tue/Wed/Sat/Sun; Thu/Fri closed. Source: NPS Visitor Centers feed
- Active alerts: High crowds & park capacity; parking areas may close when full, most often 8 am–3 pm on weekends. Source: NPS alert https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/hours.htm
- Weather (Soledad, west entrance corridor): current ~46°F clear; 3‑day forecast highs 65–71°F, lows 36–43°F, sunny.
  - 12/1: 68.7°F / 36.3°F (sunny)
  - 12/2: 70.9°F / 42.6°F (sunny)
  - 12/3: 65.1°F / 38.5°F (sunny)
  - Source: WeatherAPI via tool for Soledad, last updated 2025‑12‑01 01:15 local
- Bottom line: Excellent weather and scenery; arrive before 8 am on weekends or go midweek to avoid capacity closures.

Very popular but requires planning

Muir Woods National Monument (code: muwo)
- Distance: ~11 miles north of the Golden Gate Bridge (NPS). Source: https://www.nps.gov/muwo/index.htm
- Hours: Open daily; winter core hours 8:00 am–5:00 pm (NPS). Source: same page
- Key alerts:
  - Parking reservations required for all personal vehicles and shuttle riders: https://www.gomuirwoods.com and “Know Before You Go”: https://www.nps.gov/muwo/planyourvisit/know-before-you-go.htm (NPS alert updated 12/17/2024)
  - No cell service or Wi‑Fi (NPS alert). Auto‑theft precautions advised (NPS GGNRA link in alert)
- Weather (Mill Valley): current ~45°F, overcast; 3‑day forecast highs 56–64°F, lows 41–47°F, mostly sunny/partly cloudy. Source: WeatherAPI via tool for Mill Valley, last updated 2025‑12‑01 01:15 local
- Bottom line: Great redwoods very close to SF, but you must book parking/shuttle in advance; expect crowds; keep valuables with you.

Iconic but less suitable this week if you want minimal closures or warmer weather

Yosemite National Park (code: yose)
- Access/alerts:
  - Tioga Road (Hwy 120 through the park) and Glacier Point Road: closed due to snow. Source: NPS roads https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/wroads.htm (alert updated 11/21/2025)
  - Mist Trail/John Muir Trail blasting closures on some weekdays limit access to Vernal & Nevada Falls (no access to tops during closures). Source: NPS alert (updated 11/26/2025)
- Fee: $35/vehicle (7 days). Source: NPS https://www.nps.gov/yose/index.htm
- Distance from SF: straight‑line ≈156 miles (from NPS coordinates). Driving routes vary; allow extra time in winter conditions.
- Weather (Yosemite Valley/Yosemite Village):
  - Current ~27°F, clear; forecast highs 38–49°F, lows down to ~24°F; sunny. Dates 12/1–12/3. Source: WeatherAPI via tool, last updated 2025‑12‑01 01:15 local
- Bottom line: Cold with significant high‑country/road closures; still beautiful, but not the simplest choice for a quick, low‑risk trip right now.

Sequoia & Kings Canyon National Parks (code: seki)
- Access/alerts:
  - Winter closures: Mineral King Road; Hwy 180 beyond Grant Grove to Cedar Grove; Panoramic Point Road. Some damaged roads (Middle Fork, Redwood Canyon, South Fork, Crystal Cave) remain closed. Source: NPS road conditions https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/road-conditions.htm (updated 11/23/2025 and 9/11/2025)
- Fee: $35/vehicle (7 days). Source: NPS https://www.nps.gov/seki/index.htm
- Visitor facilities open year‑round in the foothills: Foothills Visitor Center typically daily 8:00–5:00; Giant Forest Museum typically daily 9:00–6:00 (hours may vary seasonally). Source: NPS visitor centers
- Weather (Three Rivers – foothills): current ~47°F, mostly cloudy; forecast highs 61–64°F, lows 36–41°F, sunny. Source: WeatherAPI via tool, last updated 2025‑12‑01 01:15 local
- Bottom line: Pleasant foothill weather, but many marquee high‑country areas and roads are closed for winter.

Redwood National and State Parks (code: redw)
- Distance from SF: 325 miles; 6–7 hours (NPS). Source: NPS directions https://www.nps.gov/redw/planyourvisit/directions.htm
- Access/alerts: Newton B. Drury Scenic Parkway closed to vehicles for maintenance Dec 1–3; open to pedestrians/bicyclists (NPS alert updated 11/24/2025).
- Visitor centers: Crescent City Info Center 9:00–5:00 summer / 9:00–4:00 winter; Hiouchi Visitor Center winter 10:00–4:00, closed Wed/Thu. Source: NPS visitor centers
- Weather (Crescent City): current ~45°F, clear; forecast highs 58–59°F, lows 43–47°F, sunny. Source: WeatherAPI via tool, last updated 2025‑12‑01 01:15 local
- Bottom line: Excellent weather and world‑class redwoods, but it’s a long drive. Minor temporary parkway vehicle closure Dec 1–3.

Lassen Volcanic National Park (code: lavo)
- Access/alerts: Main park road (Hwy 89) closed for winter at Kohm Yah‑mah‑nee Visitor Center and at Devastated Area; some routes impassable due to snow/mud; lingering hazards from 2021 Dixie Fire in some areas. Source: NPS alerts and weather page https://www.nps.gov/lavo/planyourvisit/weather.htm
- Fee: $30/vehicle standard (winter discount $10 when applicable). Source: NPS https://www.nps.gov/lavo/index.htm
- Weather (Mineral, CA): current ~36°F, foggy; 3‑day forecast highs 44–56°F, lows 26–36°F, sunny. Source: WeatherAPI via tool, last updated 2025‑12‑01 01:15 local
- Bottom line: Significant road closure limits park access in winter; not ideal if you want easy touring now.

Visitor centers at a glance (for the two recommended choices)
- Point Reyes — Bear Valley Visitor Center: daily 9:30–5:00. Source: NPS link above
