Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'redw'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 3639 tokens): - Name: Redwood National and State Parks (code: redw)
- URL: https://www.nps.gov/redw/index.htm
- Designation: National and State Parks
- State: CA
- Description: Renowned for the world’s tallest trees, with landscapes from prairies and oak woodlands to rivers and rugged coastline. An ancient homeland supporting people for thousands of years; jointly managed by the National Park Service and California State Parks to protect and restore resources for public enjoyment, learning, and inspiration.

Weather
- Generally cool and damp; dress in layers and expect wet conditions.
- Typical coastal temperatures year-round: mid-40s°F (7°C) to mid-60s°F (18°C); summer can be foggy with occasional highs in low 70s°F (20°C).
- Winters are cooler with significant rain; October–April averages 60–80 inches of rainfall across the region.

Directions
- Location: Northernmost coastal California near the Oregon border; park complex spans ~60 miles with four visitor centers from north to south.
- Drive times: 6–7 hours (325 mi) north of San Francisco; 6 hours (330 mi) south of Portland, OR; 4 hours (170 mi) west of Redding, CA.
- Directions page: http://www.nps.gov/redw/planyourvisit/directions.htm

