Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'muwo'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 1613 tokens): SUMMARIZED CONTENT:
- Name: Muir Woods National Monument (code: muwo)
- Designation: National Monument
- State: CA
- Website: https://www.nps.gov/muwo/index.htm
- Description: Old-growth coast redwood forest along Redwood Creek, protected since 1908. A refuge and living laboratory highlighting our connection to the landscape.

Location
- Coordinates: 37.89658027, -122.5808047
- Address: Muir Woods National Monument, 1 Muir Woods Rd, Mill Valley, CA 94941

Weather
- Typical temps: 40–70°F (4–21°C); dress in layers.
- Late Oct–early May: cool, possible rain.
- Summer (Jun–Aug): generally cool and dry; heavy morning fog, clears by afternoon.
- Fall (Sep–Oct): often warmest.

Directions
- From San Francisco: 11 miles north of Golden Gate Bridge. Hwy 101 N → Mill Valley/Highway 1/Stinson Beach exit → follow signs to Hwy 1 → Muir Woods.
- From the north: Hwy 580/Richmond–San Rafael Bridge W → Hwy 101 S → Stinson Beach/Mill Valley exit → follow signs to Hwy 1 → Muir Woods.
- Vehicle restrictions: No vehicles over 35 ft. Vehicles over 17 ft require oversized parking.
- Directions page: http://www.nps.gov/muwo/planyourvisit/directions.htm

Operating Hours
- Open daily, year-round; may close for inclement weather/hazardous conditions.
- Core winter hours: 8:00 AM–5:00 PM daily.
- Spring–fall: open later with more daylight.
- Closure updates posted on website and social media.

Contacts
- Phone: 415-561-2850
- Email: goga_muwo_socialmedia@nps.gov

Fees/Passes
- Entrance fees: none listed.
- Entrance passes: none listed.

Topics
- Animals; Birds; Fish; Forests and Woodlands; Coniferous Forests; River and Riparian; Trails; Unique Species; Endangered

Activities
- Food/Dining; Guided Tours; Hiking; Junior Ranger Program; Wildlife Watching; Birdwatching; Shopping; Bookstore/Park Store

