Tool `National Parks:getVisitorCenters` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'yose,seki,redw,lavo,pinn,pore,muwo', 'limit': 50} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 26230 tokens): Summary of visitor centers (name — parkCode)

- Bear Gulch Nature Center — pinn
  - What: Small interpretive center with park film; rangers on hand for questions.
  - Where: East side, Bear Gulch Day Use Area. Coordinates: 36.4813626, -121.1808052
  - Hours: Mon/Tue/Wed/Sat/Sun 9:00–4:00; Thu/Fri closed.
  - Contacts: (831) 389-4486 ext. 4235; Pinn_visitor_information@nps.gov

- Bear Valley Visitor Center — pore
  - What: Primary VC; orientation to roads/trails; exhibits; A/V programs on request; bookstore; beach fire permits.
  - Where: ~30 mi N of San Francisco; <1 mi off Hwy 1 on Bear Valley Rd. Address: 1 Bear Valley Rd, Point Reyes Station, CA 94956. Coordinates: 38.0411221, -122.8003357
  - Hours: Daily 9:30–5:00; closed Dec 25; usually closes 2 pm on Thanksgiving.
  - Contacts: 415-464-5100; pore_info@nps.gov. Info: https://www.nps.gov/pore/planyourvisit/visitorcenters.htm#bearvalleyvc

- Big Oak Flat Information Station — yose
  - What: Information desk, wilderness permits, Yosemite Conservancy bookstore. Winter self-registration permits (Crane Flat/Tioga Rd trailheads only) on porch. Bring own bear canister when closed. Accessible parking. Wilderness permits required for overnight trips.
  - Where: Near Big Oak Flat Entrance on Big Oak Flat Rd (Hwy 120 from west). Coordinates: 37.8003402, -119.8754342
  - Hours: Approx late May–early Oct, daily 8:00–5:00.
  - Contacts: 209-372-0200; yose_web_manager@nps.gov

- Cedar Grove Visitor Center — seki
  - What: Historic cabin VC; info, maps; potable water; accessible restrooms; ranger program venues. Summer-only; may close for lunch; hours/dates may vary.
  - Where: Hwy 180, 30 mi E of Grant Grove; next to Sentinel Campground. Address: Northside Dr, Kings Canyon NP, CA 93633. Coordinates: 36.7909602, -118.6711346
  - Hours: Typically late May–mid-Sept; standard 9:00–5:00.
  - Contacts: 559-565-3341; fax 559-565-3730; SEKI_Information@nps.gov. Info: http://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/visitorcenters.htm

- Crescent City Information Center — redw
  - What: In park HQ; picnic area; retail.
  - Where: Corner of 2nd & K St, downtown Crescent City. Address: 1111 2nd St, Crescent City, CA 95531. Coordinates: 41.7528096, -124.1940417
  - Hours: Summer daily 9:00–5:00; Winter daily 9:00–4:00.
  - Contacts: (707) 464-6101; redw_information@nps.gov. Info: https://home.nps.gov/redw/planyourvisit/visitorcenters.htm#CP_JUMP_281933

- Foothills Visitor Center — seki
  - What: Info, maps, books/gifts, water, restrooms; exhibits on foothills ecology/human history. Year-round except closures; hours vary. Self-issue wilderness permits (non-quota season) outside Wilderness Office.
  - Where: Generals Hwy, 1 mi N of Ash Mountain Entrance. Address: 47050 Generals Hwy, Three Rivers, CA 93271. Coordinates: 36.4910724, -118.8255907
  - Hours: Typically daily 8:00–5:00.
  - Contacts: 559-565-3341; fax 559-565-3730; SEKI_Information@nps.gov. Info: http://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/visitorcenters.htm

- Giant Forest Museum — seki
  - What: In historic market building; info, maps, books/gifts, water, restrooms; hands-on exhibits on giant sequoia ecology. Year-round except closures; self-issue permits in plaza (non-quota season).
  - Where: Generals Hwy, 16 mi N of Ash Mountain Entrance. Address: Mile 16, Generals Hwy, Sequoia NP, CA 93262. Coordinates: 36.5646878, -118.7726831
  - Hours: Typically daily 9:00–6:00; may vary.
  - Contacts: 559-565-3341; fax 559-565-3730; SEKI_Information@nps.gov. Info: http://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/visitorcenters.htm

- Hiouchi Visitor Center — redw
  - What: Northernmost VC; exhibits on Tolowa culture/art and redwood ecology; info; junior ranger; bookstore/retail.
  - Where: 9 mi E of Crescent City on Hwy 199. Address: 1600 US Hwy 199, Hiouchi, CA 95531. Coordinates: 41.7967724, -124.0818236
  - Hours: Summer daily 9:00–5:00; Winter 10:00–4:00, closed Wed/Thu. Closed Thanksgiving, Christmas, New Year’s Day.
  - Contacts: (707) 464-6101; redw_information@nps.
