- Paper ID: 2511.23477v1 | Title: Video-CoM: Interactive Video Reasoning via Chain of Manipulations | Authors: Hanoona Rasheed; Mohammed Zumri; Muhammad Maaz; Ming-Hsuan Yang; Fahad Shahbaz Khan; Salman Khan | Area: cs.CV | Date: 2025-11-28
  - Problem: Most MLLMs “think about videos” passively after a single encoding, creating a semantic bottleneck and shallow visual reasoning.
  - Paradigm: Interactive Video Reasoning—models “think with videos” via a Chain of Manipulations (CoM), iteratively performing visual actions to gather/verify evidence.
  - Data/Training: Video CoM Instruct (18K instruction-tuning samples) for multi-step manipulation reasoning; reinforcement learning via reasoning-aware GRPO with step-level reasoning rewards (not just sparse answer rewards).
  - Results: Strong performance on 9 video reasoning benchmarks; +3.6% average over recent SOTA while using only 25K SFT and 3K GRPO samples; better accuracy and interpretability.
  - Code: https://github.com/mbzuai-oryx/Video-CoM

- Paper ID: 2511.23476v1 | Title: Thinking by Doing: Building Efficient World Model Reasoning in LLMs via Multi-turn Interaction | Authors: Bao Shu; Yan Cai; Jianjian Sun; Chunrui Han; En Yu; Liang Zhao; Jingcheng Hu; Yinmin Zhang; Haoran Lv; Yuang Peng; Zheng Ge; Xiangyu Zhang; Daxin Jiang; Xiangyu Yue | Area: cs.AI | Date: 2025-11-28
  - Goal: Enable LLM agents to internalize world models efficiently through active, multi-turn interaction without rigid, pre-defined reasoning structures.
  - Method (WMAct): 
    - Reward rescaling based on action efficacy to reduce redundancy and incentivize purposeful interactions.
    - Interaction frequency annealing to progressively limit allowed turns, pushing the model to internalize dynamics and rely less on external cues.
  - Results: On Sokoban, Maze, and Taxi, achieves single-turn solutions where multiple interactions were previously needed; strong transfer to complex environments; improved performance on reasoning benchmarks.

- Paper ID: 2511.23475v1 | Title: AnyTalker: Scaling Multi-Person Talking Video Generation with Interactivity Refinement | Authors: Zhizhou Zhong; Yicheng Ji; Zhe Kong; Yiying Liu; Jiarui Wang; Jiasun Feng; Lupeng Liu; Xiangyi Wang; Yanjia Li; Yuqing She; Ying Qin; Huan Li; Shuiyang Mao; Wei Liu; Wenhan Luo | Area: cs.CV | Date: 2025-11-28
  - Problem: Audio-driven multi-person talking video generation is hampered by data scarcity and difficulty in maintaining coherent interactivity across multiple identities.
  - Approach: Extensible multi-stream diffusion-transformer architecture with identity-aware attention that iteratively processes identity–audio pairs, scaling to arbitrary numbers of identities.
  - Training: Relies primarily on single-person videos to learn speaking patterns, with limited real multi-person clips to refine interactivity; introduces a metric and dataset for evaluating natura


