- Thinking by Doing: Building Efficient World Model Reasoning in LLMs via Multi-turn Interaction (cs.AI)
  - Authors: Bao Shu; Yan Cai; Jianjian Sun; Chunrui Han; En Yu; Liang Zhao; Jingcheng Hu; Yinmin Zhang; Haoran Lv; Yuang Peng; Zheng Ge; Xiangyu Zhang; Daxin Jiang; Xiangyu Yue. Date: 2025-11-28. arXiv:2511.23476v1.
  - Problem: LLM agents need robust world-model reasoning; existing methods enforce rigid reasoning, hindering active learning and efficiency.
  - Approach: WMAct—internalize world models via efficient, active multi-turn interaction without rigid structures.
    - Reward rescaling: adjusts outcome rewards by action efficacy to reduce redundancy and encourage purposeful interaction.
    - Interaction frequency annealing: gradually reduces max interaction turns to force condensed learning and internalization (less reliance on environment cues).
  - Results: On Sokoban, Maze, Taxi, WMAct enables solving tasks in single turns that previously needed multiple interactions; shows strong transfer to more complex environments and boosts reasoning benchmarks.

