  authors: Muhammad Maaz; Hanoona Rasheed; Fahad Shahbaz Khan; Salman Khan
  source/category: arXiv cs.CV
  published_date: 2025-11-28
  urls: abs http://arxiv.org/abs/2511.23478v1 | pdf https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.23478v1
  citations: 0
  problem: Current video reasoning MLLMs produce convincing but logically inconsistent or weakly grounded “thinking.”
  diagnostics: Introduces two metrics:
    - Think Answer Consistency (TAC): alignment between reasoning trace and final answer.
    - Video Attention Score (VAS): reliance on visual (vs textual) evidence in reasoning.
  findings: Across 11 video reasoning benchmarks, existing models over-rely on linguistic priors over visual content.
  method: Two-stage post-training:
    - Timestamp-aware supervised fine-tuning (SFT).
    - GRPO (Group Relative Policy Optimization) with a new Temporal Alignment Reward (TAR) to promote temporally aligned, causally coherent reasoning.
  results: Video-R2 improves TAC, VAS, and accuracy consistently across multiple video benchmarks; better temporal grounding yields more accurate, trustworthy video understanding.
  notes: Code, dataset, and model to be open-sourced.

- paper_id: 2511.23477v1
