  citations: 0
  problem: Typical MLLMs “think about videos” (single-pass encoding + text-only reasoning), causing a semantic bottleneck and shallow spatio-temporal reasoning.
  paradigm: Interactive Video Reasoning—models “think with videos” by iteratively manipulating visual inputs.
  method: Video-CoM uses a Chain of Manipulations (CoM) to iteratively perform visual actions for evidence gathering/refinement. Training:
