Tool `Hugging Face:get-paper-info` with Parameter {'arxiv_id': '2409.12191'} on Hugging Face succeeded. Result (summarized from 81532 tokens): Title: Qwen2-VL: Enhancing Vision-Language Model’s Perception of the World at Any Resolution
Paper link: https://huggingface.co/papers/2409.12191
Code: https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen2-VL

What it is:
- Qwen2-VL is an upgraded vision-language model (VLM) series that departs from fixed input resolutions and improves multimodal perception for images and videos.

Key innovations:
- Naive Dynamic Resolution (NDR): Processes images at varying resolutions into different numbers of visual tokens, adapting token count to content/resolution. This yields more efficient, accurate visual representations and better aligns with human perception.
- Multimodal Rotary Position Embedding (M-RoPE): Extends rotary position embeddings to jointly handle positional information across text, images, and videos, improving cross-modal fusion.
- Unified image–video paradigm: A single processing pipeline for both images and videos, enhancing general visual perception and simplifying training/inference.
- Scaling laws for LVLMs: Systematic study of scaling both model size (2B, 8B, 72B parameters) and training data volume to characterize capability growth.

Capabilities and results:
- Strong, competitive performance across a wide range of multimodal benchmarks.
- The largest model, Qwen2-VL-72B, reports results comparable to leading models (e.g., GPT-4o, Claude 3.5 Sonnet) and outperforms other general-purpose models in many settings.

Model sizes in the series:
- 2B, 8B, and 72B parameter variants.

Availability:
- Open-source code and multiple pretrained/finetuned checkpoints are available. Representative Hugging Face models include:
  - Qwen2-VL (base/instruct):
    - Qwen/Qwen2-VL-2B, Qwen/Qwen2-VL-2B-Instruct
    - Qwen/Qwen2-VL-7B, Qwen/Qwen2-VL-7B-Instruct
    - Qwen/Qwen2-VL-72B, Qwen/Qwen2-VL-72B-Instruct
  - Qwen2.5-VL instruct (successor line referencing this work):
    - Qwen/Qwen2.5-VL-3B-Instruct
    - Qwen/Qwen2.5-VL-7B-Instruct
    - Qwen/Qwen2.5-VL-72B-Instruct
    - Quantized variants: Qwen/Qwen2.5-VL-7B-Instruct-GGUF (unsloth), Qwen/Qwen2.5-VL-7B-Instruct-AWQ, Qwen/Qwen2.5-VL-72B-Instruct-AWQ
  - Related/derivative models:
    - Qwen/QVQ-72B-Preview (finetuned from Qwen2-VL-72B)
    - Numerous Qwen3-VL models cite/trace lineage to this work (e.g., Qwen3-VL-2B/4B/8B/32B/30B MoE/235B MoE; both Instruct and Thinking; FP8/AWQ/quantized variants)

Notes:
- The dynamic-resolution design directly reduces unnecessary visual tokens for low-information regions/inputs, improving efficiency without sacrificing detail when high resolution is needed.
- M-RoPE strengthens positional coherence across modalities, which is crucial for tasks involving spatial reasoning in images and temporal reasoning in videos.

Authors (selection): Peng Wang, Shuai Bai, Sinan Tan, Shijie Wang, Zhihao Fan, Jinze Bai, Keqin Chen, Xuejing Liu, Jialin Wang, Wenbin Ge, Yang Fan, Kai Dang, Mengfei Du, Xuancheng Ren, Rui Men, Dayiheng Liu, Chang Zhou, Jingren Zhou, Junyang Lin, et al.
Tool `Hugging Face:get-paper-info` with Parameter {'arxiv_id': '2407.08083'} on Hugging Face succeeded. Result (summarized from 2342 tokens): Title: MambaVision: A Hybrid Mamba-Transformer Vision Backbone
ArXiv: 2407.08083
Authors: Ali Hatamizadeh, Jan Kautz
Paper page: https://huggingface.co/papers/2407.08083
Code: https://github.com/NVlabs/MambaVision

Core idea and contributions:
- Proposes MambaVision, a hybrid Mamba-Transformer vision backbone.
- Redesigns the Mamba formulation to more efficiently model visual features.
- Comprehensive ablation shows that adding a few self-attention blocks at the final layers substantially improves the ability to capture long-range spatial dependencies.
- Introduces a hierarchical family of MambaVision models to meet different design and deployment criteria.

Results:
- Image classification (ImageNet-1K): Achieves new state-of-the-art Top-1 accuracy and image throughput among comparable backbones.
- Downstream tasks: Outperforms comparably sized backbones on object detection, instance segmentation, and semantic segmentation on MS COCO and ADE20K.

