Tool `Hugging Face:get-paper-info` with Parameter {'arxiv_id': '2310.01377'} on Hugging Face succeeded. Result (summarized from 270963 tokens): Title: UltraFeedback: Boosting Language Models with High-quality Feedback

Authors: Ganqu Cui, Lifan Yuan, Ning Ding, Guanming Yao, Wei Zhu, Yuan Ni, Guotong Xie, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun

Problem/motivation:
- RLHF relies on high-quality preference data to align LLMs with human preferences.
- The open-source community faces a shortage of large, diverse, naturalistic preference datasets, limiting RLHF adoption and research.

Contribution:
- UltraFeedback: a large-scale, high-quality, diversified preference dataset designed to overcome data scarcity and foster RLHF/feedback learning.
- Establishes a reproducible, expandable pipeline for preference data construction.

Dataset construction:
- Compiles a diverse array of instructions and models from multiple sources to generate comparative data.
- Carefully designed annotation instructions.
- Uses GPT-4 to provide detailed feedback in both numerical and textual forms.

Models trained using UltraFeedback:
- UltraRM (reward model)
- UltraLM-13B-PPO (chat language model)
- UltraCM (critique model)

Results:
- These models outperform existing open-source baselines, achieving top performance across multiple benchmarks.

Availability:
- Paper page: https://huggingface.co/papers/2310.01377
- Data and models: https://github.com/thunlp/UltraFeedback

