Authors: Xianhang Li, Haoqin Tu, Mude Hui, Zeyu Wang, Bingchen Zhao, Junfei Xiao, Sucheng Ren, Jieru Mei, Qing Liu, Huangjie Zheng, Yuyin Zhou, Cihang Xie

Overview:
- Problem: Web-crawled image–text pairs are noisy; improving their captions boosts training for vision–language models.
- Contribution: Open-source, large-scale recaptioning of 1.3B images (DataComp-1B) using a LLaMA-3–based pipeline; release of Recap-DataComp-1B.
- Approach: Fine-tune LLaVA-1.5 powered by LLaMA-3-8B; use it to recaption 1.3B images.
- Key finding: Recaptioned data significantly improves both discriminative and generative VLMs.

Method:
- Fine-tune LLaVA-1.5 with LLaMA-3-8B as the language backbone.
- Use the resulting vision-language model to generate higher-quality, semantically aligned captions for 1.3B images from DataComp-1B.
- Train downstream models on the recaptioned dataset (Recap-DataComp-1B) and evaluate.

Results:
- Discriminative models (e.g., CLIP): Better zero-shot performance on cross-modal retrieval.
- Generative models (e.g., text-to-image Diffusion Transformers): Stronger text-image alignment, noticeably better adherence to complex prompts.

Resources:
- Paper page: https://huggingface.co/papers/2406.08478
- Project page: https://www.haqtu.me/Recap-Datacomp-1B/
- arXiv tag referenced: 2406.08478 (arxiv_id not provided in metadata)

