1) Video-R2: Reinforcing Consistent and Grounded Reasoning in Multimodal Language Models
- Authors: Muhammad Maaz; Hanoona Rasheed; Fahad Shahbaz Khan; Salman Khan
- Problem: MLLMs often produce convincing but logically inconsistent and weakly grounded video reasoning, over-relying on linguistic priors.
- Diagnostics:
  - Think Answer Consistency (TAC): alignment between reasoning and final answer.
  - Video Attention Score (VAS): dependency of reasoning on visual vs textual cues.
- Evidence: Across 11 video reasoning benchmarks, current models lean heavily on language priors over visual content.
- Method: Two-stage post-training pipeline:
  - Timestamp-aware supervised fine-tuning (SFT) to improve temporal precision.
  - Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) with a new Temporal Alignment Reward (TAR) to encourage temporally aligned, causally coherent reasoning.
- Results: Consistently higher TAC, VAS, and accuracy across benchmarks; demonstrates that better temporal alignment and coherence yield more accurate, trustworthy video understanding.
- Resources: Code, dataset, and model to be open-sourced.
- Category: cs.CV. Published: 2025-11-28. Citations: 0.

2) Video-CoM: Interactive Video Reasoning via Chain of Manipulations
- Authors: Hanoona Rasheed; Mohammed Zumri; Muhammad Maaz; Ming-Hsuan Yang; Fahad Shahbaz Khan; Salman Khan
- Problem: Most MLLMs “think about videos” only once post-encoding, creating a semantic bottleneck (no rewatch/refocus/verification), limiting fine-grained spatiotemporal reasoning.
- Paradigm: Interactive Video Reasoning—models “think with videos” via active, iterative visual actions.
- Model: Video-CoM performs a Chain of Manipulations (CoM) to gather and refine visual evidence.
- Data: Video-CoM Instruct (18K instruction-tuning samples) curated for multi-step manipulation reasoning.
- RL: Reasoning-aware GRPO with step-level reasoning rewards (not just sparse answer rewards) to guide grounded, consistent reasoning.
- Results: Strong performance on 9 video reasoning benchmarks; +3.6% average over recent SOTA while training on only 25K SFT + 3K GRPO video samples. Ablations show improved accuracy and interpretability.
- Code: https://github.com/mbzuai-oryx/Video-CoM
- Category: cs.CV. Published: 2025-11-28. Citations: 0.

3) Thinking by Doing: Building Efficient World Model Reasoning in LLMs via Multi-turn Interaction
- Authors: Bao Shu; Yan Cai; Jianjian Sun; Chunrui Han; En Yu; Liang Zhao; Jingcheng Hu; Yinmin Zhang; Haoran Lv; Yuang Peng; Zheng Ge; Xiangyu Zhang; Daxin Jiang; Xiangyu Yue
- Problem: Rigid, pre-structured reasoning in interactive LLM agents hinders active learning and efficient world model internalization.
- Framework: WMAct—world-model internalization through efficient interaction and active reasoning, letting the model “shape thinking by doing.”
- Key mechanisms:
  - Reward rescaling: adjusts outcome reward by action efficacy to reduce redundancy and promote purposeful interactions.
  - Interaction frequency annealing: gradually lowers the maximum allowed interaction turns, pushing the model to condense learning and internalize dynamics instead of over-relying on environment feedback.
- Results: On Sokoban, Maze, and Taxi, WMAct enables single-turn solutions where multiple interactions were previously needed; shows strong transferability and boosts across reasoning benchmarks.
- Category: cs.AI. Published: 2025-11-28. Citations: 0.

