--- Summary of Round 1 ---
Tool `Paper Search:search_pubmed` with Parameter {'query': '("Artificial Intelligence"[Mesh] OR "Machine Learning"[Mesh] OR "artificial intelligence"[Title/Abstract] OR "machine learning"[Title/Abstract]) AND (outcomes OR "patient outcomes" OR mortality OR "length of stay" OR readmission OR "clinical trial" OR randomized OR "real-world") AND ("2019/01/01"[Date - Publication] : "2025/12/31"[Date - Publication])', 'max_results': 25} on Paper Search succeeded. Result (summarized from 9069 tokens): Here’s a concise synthesis of the key points across the included papers:

- Diagnosis and treatment of coronary artery disease in CKD (Dod; Yadav; Jovin): CKD markedly raises CAD risk through intertwined pathways (inflammation, oxidative stress, lipid abnormalities). Management must simultaneously reduce cardiovascular risk and protect renal function; therapeutic decision-making is complex.

- UQCR10 and TNNT1 as sarcopenia biomarkers (Sun et al.): Integrated transcriptomics and machine learning identified UQCR10 and TNNT1 as novel diagnostic biomarkers for sarcopenia, addressing gaps in molecular diagnosis and potential targeted therapy.

- HFpEF: pathophysiology to tech-enabled management (Pozzi et al.): HFpEF accounts for ~50% of HF; comorbidity-driven complexity blunts effectiveness of many HFrEF therapies. Recent promise with MRAs, SGLT2 inhibitors, and GLP-1 RAs. AI can phenotype risk; remote monitoring may optimize limited resources. Review emphasizes emerging evidence and strategies.

- OBSCN in gastric cancer (Chen et al.): Multi-omics links OBSCN expression to immunotherapy outcomes; higher OBSCN correlates with worse DFS. Tumor microbes (e.g., Fusobacterium) may regulate miRNAs targeting OBSCN. OBSCN mutations associate with higher intratumoral microbiome diversity, elevated TMB, and better ICI response. ML models based on OBSCN mutation–related gene signatures accurately predict ICI response. OBSCN is a nexus among genomics, microbiome, and immune infiltration.

- Pediatric moderate-to-severe TBI CT scoring and ML (Diao; Liang): Assesses prognostic performance of four CT scoring systems and proposes a simplified, interpretable ML model to predict outcomes in pediatric TBI.

- Predicting methotrexate side effects in RA with explainable ML (Jang et al.): Develops interpretable ML models (with XAI) to predict MTX-related GI, hepatic, and marrow toxicity using nationwide multicenter real-world data for individualized risk stratification.

- TRIPOD+AI adherence in ML models for SGA/FGR (Zamagni et al.): Systematic review of ML for predicting SGA/FGR, evaluating methodological rigor and reporting quality against TRIPOD+AI guidelines; underscores need for standardized, transparent reporting.

- Digital health integration in CKD (Deng; Xue; Methakanjanasak): Telemedicine, wearables, mHealth, and AI-DSS support early detection, remote monitoring, self-management, and personalized care. Real-time tracking (renal biomarkers, BP, adherence) enables predictive analytics; EHR integration supports coordinated care. Challenges: scalability, privacy, literacy, regulation. Calls for interoperable, patient-centric ecosystems and multicenter validation—toward precision nephrology.

- Long COVID predicts MG exacerbation; ML risk stratification (Li et al.): Prospective cohort shows Long COVID independently predicts exacerbations in myasthenia gravis; ML helps identify high-risk patients for proactive care.

- Psoriasis relapse after IL-17 blockade (Wang et al.): Pre-treatment expression of KLRB1 and IL12RB1 predicts time to relapse after therapy cessation, informing individualized treatment planning.

- Digital dentistry scoping review (Lam et al.): 407 studies mapped. Domains: prevention/diagnosis (preventive dentistry n=39; cariology n=26; periodontology n=16) and management/care (prosthodontics n=127; OMFS n=112; orthodontics n=26; perioperative n=61). Encompasses AI, CAD/CAM, computer-assisted surgery, imaging, teledentistry. Stresses critical appraisal, clinician judgment, standardized high-quality data, and real-world impact. Informs 2025 FDI Policy Statement.

