Key studies and protocols
- Meta-analysis (major abdominal surgery): Assessed whether HPI-guided management improves postoperative outcomes; included post hoc analyses of IOH metrics in adults undergoing major abdominal surgery. Findings not reported in abstract.
- RCT protocol (orthopedic/trauma, noninvasive monitoring): Tests continuous, noninvasive AI-supported HPI system to reduce IOH incidence/severity and complications (AKI, MINS, delirium) vs standard intermittent monitoring; addresses “blind gaps” of noninvasive NIBP. No results yet.
- RCT (elderly pancreaticoduodenectomy): Tests whether HPI reduces IOH in high-risk elderly patients (MAP <65 mmHg threshold). Results not in abstract.
- Feasibility study (elective noncardiac surgery): Evaluates Acumen HPI “Smart Alerts” and trends to improve compliance with goal-directed hemodynamic therapy (GDHT) algorithms; hypothesis that smart prompts improve adherence. Results not in abstract.
- Systematic review/meta-analysis: Evaluates whether HPI-guided strategies reduce major perioperative complications and IOH; acknowledges controversy over HPI’s impact on complications. Results not in abstract.
- Systematic review/meta-analysis (cardiac and noncardiac): Appraises whether HPI meaningfully improves prediction/prevention of IOH and postoperative outcomes (AKI, MI, stroke, mortality). Results not in abstract.
- Systematic review, meta-analysis, and trial sequential analysis (noncardiac surgery): Determines effectiveness of HPI for adult noncardiac surgeries; prospectively registered (PROSPERO CRD42024571931). Results not in abstract.
- RCT (robot-assisted radical prostatectomy): Compares standard goal-directed therapy vs HPI-guided GDT to maintain stable BP during RARP and potentially improve outcomes. Results not in abstract.
- Single-center RCT (prone spine fusion): 85 enrolled; 77 analyzed (39 HPI). Primary outcome (TWA of IOH) not significantly different: 0.10 mmHg [0.05, 0.23] vs 0.15 mmHg [0.09, 0.37]; p=0.088. Total duration of hypotension per patient lower with HPI: 4 min [0.5, 12.2] vs 11.2 min [2.6, 20.1]; p=0.019. Postoperative complication rates similar. ClinicalTrials.gov: NCT05341167.
- RCT protocol (head and neck free flap): Tests HPI’s impact on incidence/severity of IOH and potential effects on mortality, morbidity, and flap outcomes in long, complex microvascular surgery. No results.
- Clinical perspective: Reviews reliability of HPI validation and whether MAP can be used interchangeably with HPI; notes debates about prior validation robustness.
- Pilot study (lung surgery with single-lung ventilation): Tests AI-guided goal-directed treatment vs standard care to reduce frequency/duration/severity of IOH and potentially AKI. Results not in abstract.
- RCT protocol (major abdominal surgery): Compares perioperative hypotension rates across hemodynamic monitoring strategies, including HPI, in high-risk abdominal procedures. No results.
- Systematic review/meta-analysis of RCTs: Quantifies HPI effects on IOH outcomes (time-weighted average [TWA], area under hypotension threshold [AUHT], incidence, duration). Results not in abstract.
- HYPE-2 RCT (cardiac surgery + ICU): Tests HPI with diagnostic guidance to reduce hypotension during and after cardiac surgery; prior HPI use largely in noncardiac settings. Results not in abstract.
- Systematic review/meta-analysis (ML in perioperative care): Synthesizes effects of ML-driven interventions (including HPI) on perioperative outcomes. Results not in abstract.
