Evidence across randomized trials, health-technology assessments, real-world surveillance, and economic models supports encorafenib (BRAFTOVI) plus binimetinib (MEKTOVI) as a standard targeted option for BRAF V600–mutant melanoma. Long-term COLUMBUS data (5–7 years) show durable benefit versus single-agent BRAF inhibitors, with acceptable tolerability. Ongoing work explores adjuvant use in stage IIB/IIC melanoma and broader indications. Multiple cost-effectiveness analyses and the NICE appraisal generally support its value relative to other BRAF/MEK combinations, though head-to-head efficacy differences versus dabrafenib/trametinib are not statistically definitive in network meta-analyses. A Japanese post-marketing study is assessing real-world safety/effectiveness.

