Tool `Paper Search:search_pubmed` with Parameter {'query': 'ctDNA BRAF V600E melanoma targeted therapy kinetics survival predictive biomarker', 'max_results': 10} on Paper Search succeeded. Result: [{"paper_id":"40250457","title":"Clinical validation of droplet digital PCR assays in detecting BRAF","authors":"Syeda MM; Long GV; Garrett J; Atkinson V; Santinami M; Schadendorf D; Hauschild A; Millward M; Mandala M; Chiarion-Sileni V; Smylie M; Manikhas GM; Dummer R; Wiggins JM; Ali S; Adnaik SB; Tan M; Dajee M; Polsky D","abstract":"Cell-free, circulating tumour DNA (ctDNA) is an established measure of minimal residual disease; however, it is not utilised in melanoma management. We investigated whether ctDNA measurements could predict survival outcomes during adjuvant targeted therapy or placebo treatment in stage III melanoma, thereby identifying patients at high risk and low risk of recurrence.","doi":"10.1016/S1470-2045(25)00139-1","published_date":"2025-01-01T00:00:00","pdf_url":"","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40250457/","source":"pubmed","updated_date":"2025-01-01T00:00:00","categories":"","keywords":"","citations":0,"references":"","extra":""}]


