2025-12-01 11:42:11,283 - agent.executor - INFO - Decision: CONTINUE. Reasoning: The task requires evidence-backed data on solar activity over the last month and its relationship to geomagnetic storms, plus visuals, ideally around Los Angeles. The task is not complete yet because we need to collect recent solar event timelines and storm data, then correlate them and select representative imagery. In this round, we will pull all relevant NASA DONKI datasets for the past 30 days (CME, solar flares, SEPs, GST, HSS, MPC, RBE) and WSA–Enlil simulations for the last week to identify impactful events and provide visualizations. We will also retrieve EPIC available dates (natural and enhanced) to target potential global aurora imagery later, and fetch recent Landsat imagery over Los Angeles to assess available visuals for that region. These independent data retrievals can run in parallel without dependencies. After this, we will analyze and correlate event timestamps with geomagnetic storms, and select/produce visuals (e.g., WSA–Enlil frames, EPIC aurora dates, and LA imagery) in the next round.
