What I pulled together (data sources used)
- NASA/CCMC DONKI event catalogs: CMEs, solar flares, solar energetic particles (SEPs), geomagnetic storms (GST), high‑speed streams (HSS), magnetopause crossings (MPC), radiation belt enhancements (RBE), WSA–Enlil model runs, and weekly reports.
- APOD for curated, license‑clear imagery that directly references the mid‑November auroral activity.
- Note: Attempts to fetch NASA Earth Imagery tiles centered on Los Angeles (34.0522, −118.2437) returned API errors during this session; alternatives are provided below.

Executive snapshot (Nov 1–Dec 1, 2025)
- Solar drivers
  - CMEs: 172 cataloged CMEs (many east/northeast limb; several Earth‑directed) with speeds in the sampled set from ~250–780 km/s.
  - Flares: 45 flares, including multiple M‑class bursts (e.g., M1.0 on Nov 2; M1.6, M5.0, M3.2, M2.9 on Nov 3) and an X1.9 on Dec 1 indicating continued high activity.
  - SEPs: 23 SEP events, strongly clustered on Nov 10–11, tied to M‑class flares and CMEs.
  - HSS (coronal hole streams): 4 events (Nov 6, 20, 24, 28), interacting with CME effects at times.
- Geomagnetic response (Kp/G‑scale; strongest first)
  - Nov 12 00:00Z: Kp peaked at 8.67 then 8.33 (G4 severe). Related CMEs on Nov 7, 9, 10; IPS/MPC confirm impact/compression.
  - Nov 12 18:00Z: Kp up to 7.33 (G3 strong) from additional Nov 10–11 CMEs.
  - Nov 8 00:00Z: Kp ~6.33 (G2–G3) from a Nov 5 CME.
  - Nov 5 21:00Z: Kp 6.0–6.67 (G2–G3) from a Nov 3 CME.
- Magnetospheric/satellite environment
  - Magnetopause crossings: Nov 6, Nov 12, Nov 13 (dayside compression inward toward GEO), consistent with enhanced satellite risk windows.
  - Radiation Belt Enhancements: Nov 8, 13, 19, 25 (elevated internal/external charging risk periods).
  - WSA–Enlil model runs around Nov 9–13 show multiple CME propagations consistent with the storm sequence.

How the pieces connect (event → impact chain, with DONKI references)
- Nov 3 CME → Nov 5–6 geomagnetic storm (G2–G3)
  - Geomagnetic storm: 2025‑11‑05T21:00Z; Kp 6.0 at 00:00Z, 6.67 at 06:00Z
    - DONKI: https://webtools.ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/DONKI/view/GST/42455/-1
    - Related events: 2025‑11‑03T09:36Z CME; 2025‑11‑06T03:51Z MPC confirms compression.
  - Flares around the source window included several M‑class (e.g., M1.6, M5.0, M3.2 on Nov 3).

- Nov 5 CME → Nov 8 geomagnetic storm (G2–G3)
  - Geomagnetic storm: 2025‑11‑08T00:00Z; Kp ~6.33 at 03:00Z
    - DONKI: https://webtools.ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/DONKI/view/GST/42533/-1
    - Related events: 2025‑11‑05T22:23Z CME; HSS on Nov 6 may have modulated background conditions.

- CME train (Nov 7–11) → Nov 12 severe geomagnetic storms (G4 then G3+)
  - Geomagnetic storm: 2025‑11‑12T00:00Z; Kp 8.67 at 03:00Z and 8.33 at 06:00Z (G4 severe)
    - DONKI: https://webtools.ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/DONKI/view/GST/42642/-1
    - Related events: CMEs on 2025‑11‑07 12:53Z, 2025‑11‑09 07:24Z, 2025‑11‑10 09:36Z; IPS/MPC confirm arrival/compression.
  - Follow‑on storm: 2025‑11‑12T18:00Z; Kp 6.0 at 21:00Z, 7.33 at 03:00Z on Nov 13 (G3)
    - DONKI: https://webtools.ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/DONKI/view/GST/42662/-1
    - Related events: CMEs on 2025‑11‑10 13:08Z, 2025‑11‑11 10:23Z; IPS/MPC confirm impact.

- SEP clustering (evidence of strong eruptive drivers)
  - Multiple SEP entries on Nov 10–11 tied to flares and CMEs:
    - Example: 2025‑11‑10 10:24Z SEP with related events 2025‑11‑10 08:55Z flare, 09:36Z CME
