2025-12-01 11:50:34,297 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -         The agent retrieved CMEs, solar flares, SEPs, geomagnetic storms, and related magnetospheric data for the full 30-day window, correlated the top CMEs with the four recorded storms, and clearly identified the Nov 12 G4 event as the strongest. It provided a detailed chain of event links, Kp values, and impact analysis on satellites and communications. However, it failed to produce actual Earth imagery for Los Angeles—API errors were noted and only generic or alternative visuals (APOD Florida aurora, auroral oval plots) were supplied. Out of five core subtasks (CME/flair retrieval, storm correlation, strongest event identification, LA imagery acquisition, summary of impacts with URLs), four were fully met and one was only partially met (0% for direct LA imagery), for an 80% fulfillment rate.
2025-12-01 11:50:34,297 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -       Grounding:
2025-12-01 11:50:34,297 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -         Nearly every factual claim about event timings, speeds, Kp indices, and impacts is backed by explicit DONKI tool outputs and direct URLs to CME, GST, SEP, MPC, and RBE records. Descriptions of satellite risks cite specific magnetopause crossings and radiation belt enhancements drawn from tool data. Only speculative discussion about LA-local observations (auroral visibility) lacks direct tool output, but it is clearly labeled as recommendation. Well over 90% of claims are directly grounded.
2025-12-01 11:50:34,297 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -       Tool Appropriateness:
2025-12-01 11:50:34,297 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -         The agent used the correct NASA DONKI endpoints for CMEs, flares, SEPs, storms, HSS, MPC, RBE, and WSA–Enlil simulations. It also attempted the dedicated Earth imagery API for LA. Only the EPIC date queries were irrelevant to the task, but they did not adversely affect the main analysis. About 94% of tool choices directly supported required subtasks.
2025-12-01 11:50:34,297 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -       Parameter Accuracy:
2025-12-01 11:50:34,297 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -         All required tool calls used accurate start/end dates (2025-11-01 to 2025-12-01), correct coordinate parameters for LA, and proper notification filters. Even the failed imagery calls had syntactically correct parameters. There were no incorrect or missing parameters for any successful data retrieval.
2025-12-01 11:50:34,298 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -       Dependency Awareness:
2025-12-01 11:50:34,298 - benchmark.results_formatter - INFO -         The agent first gathered all upstream solar inputs, then fetched geomagnetic responses, and only afterward attempted imagery. Correlation links (CME→storm→MPC/RBE impacts) follow the correct dependency chain. Despite an extra WSA–Enlil window fetch, about 85% of the dependency logic was executed in the right order.
