2025-12-01 12:04:43,571 - benchmark.runner - INFO - Below is a concrete, evidence-backed way to approach the analysis, followed by a side-by-side comparison of two popular APIs using their published OpenAPI specs and official docs. I’ve included specific numbers, parameter details, defaults, and links you can verify.

How to approach this (replicable, evidence-focused)
1) Pull the OpenAPI specs and count endpoints; inspect global security vs per-operation overrides.
   - Look at the top-level “security” object and each operation’s “security” (OpenAPI 3.0).
   - Extract securitySchemes to confirm the auth type (http basic vs bearer).
   - Sources you can use directly:
     - Stripe OpenAPI: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/stripe/openapi/master/openapi/spec3.json
     - Twilio REST v2010 OpenAPI: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/twilio/twilio-oai/main/spec/json/twilio_api_v2010.json
     - Twilio Messaging v1 OpenAPI: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/twilio/twilio-oai/main/spec/json/twilio_messaging_v1.json
     - For a browsable summary of any path in these specs: https://oapis.org/summary/[url-encoded-spec]/[operation-or-path]
2) For each API, verify the auth model in vendor docs and tie it to the spec’s securitySchemes.
   - Stripe Authentication: https://stripe.com/docs/api/authentication
   - Twilio REST/API key auth: https://www.twilio.com/docs/iam/keys/api-keys and HTTP Basic details: https://www.twilio.com/docs/usage/security#http-basic-authentication
3) Sample a few representative endpoints to see concrete parameter rules, defaults, and response schemas.
   - Stripe examples (from spec):
     - GET /v1/charges: limit 1–100 (default 10); created supports range filters with gt/gte/lt/lte; pagination via starting_after and ending_before.
       Source: https://oapis.org/summary/https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2Fstripe%2Fopenapi%2Fmaster%2Fopenapi%2Fspec3.json//v1/charges
     - GET /v1/customers: same pagination; email filter; test_clock filter; created range filter; default limit 10.
       Source: https://oapis.org/summary/https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2Fstripe%2Fopenapi%2Fmaster%2Fopenapi%2Fspec3.json//v1/customers
     - GET /v1/payment_intents and GET /v1/checkout/sessions: created range filters; default limit 10; cursor pagination; expand[] support.
       Sources: https://oapis.org/summary/https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2Fstripe%2Fopenapi%2Fmaster%2Fopenapi%2Fspec3.json//v1/payment_intents and //v1/checkout/sessions
   - Twilio examples (from spec):
     - POST /v1/Services (Messaging): FriendlyName required; ValidityPeriod 1–36,000 seconds (default 36,000); host https://messaging.twilio.com; security accountSid_authToken.
       Source: https://oapis.org/summary/https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2Ftwilio%2Ftwilio-oai%2Fmain%2Fspec%2Fjson%2Ftwilio_messaging_v1.json//v1/Services
     - GET/POST /v1/a2p/BrandRegistrations: PageSize 1–1000 (default 50); paginated meta fields; security accountSid_authToken.
       Source: https://oapis.org/summary/https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2Ftwilio%2Ftwilio-oai%2Fmain%2Fspec%2Fjson%2Ftwilio_messaging_v1.json//v1/a2p/BrandRegistrations
     - GET/POST /v1/Tollfree/Verifications: Status filter enum PENDING_REVIEW|IN_REVIEW|TWILIO_APPROVED|TWILIO_REJECTED; PageSize up to 1000 (default 50); security accountSid_authToken.
       Source: https://oapis.org/summary/https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2Ftwilio%2Ftwilio-oai%2Fmain%2Fspec%2Fjson%2Ftwilio_messaging_v1.json//v1/Tollfree/Verifications
     - Twilio REST v2010 Accounts (Create/List): security accountSid_authToken applies globally; POST returns fields including auth_token, sid, status; response headers include explicit CORS items.
       Source: https://oapis.org/summary/https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2Ftwilio%2Ftwilio-oai%2Fmain%2Fspec%2Fjson%2Ftwilio_api_v2010.json//2010-04-01/Accounts.json
4) Validate with a few curl calls in a test account to observe 401/200 behavior and confirm auth requirements.
5) For operational metadata depth, check for: parameter ranges/defaults, pagination patterns, enums, response schemas, examples, and headers (CORS, idempotency, webhook signing guidance in docs).

Security models and which endpoints need what auth
Stripe
- Auth scheme: Bearer token in Authorization header for all API requests.
  - “All requests must be authenticated with an API key” (Authorization: Bearer <api_key>).
  - Source: https://stripe.com/docs/api/authentication
- Connect/OAuth: When acting for a connected account, you can use OAuth tokens or a platform key with the Stripe-Account header (documented under Connect).
  - Source: https://stripe.com/docs/connect/authentication
- Idempotency: Supported for safely retrying POST/DELETE via Idempotency-Key header.
  - Source: https://stripe.com/docs/idempotency
- Webhooks: Verify event signatures using the Stripe-Signature header.
  - Source: https://stripe.com/docs/webhooks/signatures
- Endpoint coverage: The Stripe OpenAPI lists 585 endpoints at base URL https://api.stripe.com; all require authentication per the docs above.
  - Spec: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/stripe/openapi/master/openapi/spec3.json
  - Overview summary reference: https://oapis.org/summary/https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2Fstripe%2Fopenapi%2Fmaster%2Fopenapi%2Fspec3.json
Twilio (REST v2010 and Messaging v1)
- Auth scheme: HTTP Basic for API calls.
  - Username/password are either:
    - Account SID (AC...) + Auth Token, or
    - API Key SID (SK...) + API Key Secret (recommended) — both use HTTP Basic auth.
  - Sources:
    - API Keys: https://www.twilio.com/docs/iam/keys/api-keys
    - HTTP Basic details: https://www.twilio.com/docs/usage/security#http-basic-authentication
- Webhooks: Twilio signs webhooks; verify via X-Twilio-Signature.
  - Source: https://www.twilio.com/docs/usage/security#validating-requests
- Endpoint coverage and security in spec:
  - Twilio REST v2010: 197 endpoints; base https://api.twilio.com; operations carry security: accountSid_authToken (global).
    - Spec: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/twilio/twilio-oai/main/spec/json/twilio_api_v2010.json
    - Overview summary reference: https://oapis.org/summary/https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2Ftwilio%2Ftwilio-oai%2Fmain%2Fspec%2Fjson%2Ftwilio_api_v2010.json
    - Example with explicit security: /2010-04-01/Accounts.json shows Security: accountSid_authToken.
      - Source: https://oapis.org/summary/https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2Ftwilio%2Ftwilio-oai%2Fmain%2Fspec%2Fjson%2Ftwilio_api_v2010.json//2010-04-01/Accounts.json
  - Twilio Messaging v1: 57 endpoints; base https://messaging.twilio.com; security: accountSid_authToken on endpoints.
    - Spec: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/twilio/twilio-oai/main/spec/json/twilio_messaging_v1.json
    - Overview summary reference: https://oapis.org/summary/https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2Ftwilio%2Ftwilio-oai%2Fmain%2Fspec%2Fjson%2Ftwilio_messaging_v1.json
    - Examples with explicit security in the spec summaries:
      - /v1/Services: Security: accountSid_authToken
        - Source: https://oapis.org/summary/https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2Ftwilio%2Ftwilio-oai%2Fmain%2Fspec%2Fjson%2Ftwilio_messaging_v1.json//v1/Services
      - /v1/a2p/BrandRegistrations and /v1/Tollfree/Verifications: Security: accountSid_authToken
        - Sources: /v1/a2p/BrandRegistrations and /v1/Tollfree/Verifications links above
- Net: In both Twilio specs reviewed, authentication is uniformly required (HTTP Basic) across endpoints. There aren’t “public” unauthenticated endpoints in these REST APIs.

Operational metadata depth (specific examples and numbers)
Stripe (from OpenAPI spec and docs)
- Pagination is consistent across list endpoints:
  - limit integer 1–100, default 10; cursor params starting_after and ending_before.
  - Example: GET /v1/charges and GET /v1/customers show these exact numbers.
  - Sources: /v1/charges and /v1/customers spec summaries above.
- Time-based filters use range operators with deep object encoding:
  - created can be an integer timestamp or an object with gt/gte/lt/lte.
  - Sources: /v1/charges, /v1/customers, /v1/payment_intents spec summaries above.
- Expansion of nested objects via expand[] is standard across endpoints.
  - Sources: /v1/charges, /v1/payment_intents, /v1/checkout/sessions spec summaries above and docs https://stripe.com/docs/expand
- Request encoding: application/x-www-form-urlencoded for most endpoints (including GET bodies being unused).
  - Sources: /v1/charges, /v1/payment_intents, /v1/checkout/sessions summaries.
- Idempotency headers documented and enforced for POST/DELETE.
  - Source: https://stripe.com/docs/idempotency
- Webhook signature requirements documented with precise header name Stripe-Signature and verification algorithm.
  - Source: https://stripe.com/docs/webhooks/signatures
Twilio (from OpenAPI specs)
- Pagination and meta fields are explicit where applicable; Messaging endpoints expose PageSize ranges and paginated meta.
  - Example: /v1/a2p/BrandRegistrations: PageSize 1–1000 (default 50), Page, PageToken, and meta {first_page_url, next_page_url, key, page_size, ...}.
  - Source: /v1/a2p/BrandRegistrations spec summary.
- Detailed enums and defaults are specified in many endpoints.
  - Example: /v1/Services ValidityPeriod 1–36,000 with default 36,000; enum for Usecase (notifications, marketing, verification, discussion, poll, undeclared); flags for StickySender, MmsConverter, SmartEncoding.
  - Source: /v1/Services spec summary.
- Response headers (including CORS) are documented in some endpoints (e.g., Accounts, Brand Registrations, Tollfree Verifications).
  - Example: /2010-04-01/Accounts.json shows Access-Control-Allow-Origin/Methods/Headers/Credentials/Expose-Headers in responses.
  - Sources: /2010-04-01/Accounts.json and /v1/a2p/BrandRegistrations, /v1/Tollfree/Verifications spec summaries.
- Uniform security across endpoints is represented via Security: accountSid_authToken in both specs (REST v2010 and Messaging v1).
  - Sources linked above.

