Core resources and capabilities

- Accounts
  - List accounts; create subaccounts; fetch/update an account.
- Addresses
  - List/create/fetch/update/delete addresses.
- Applications
  - List/create/fetch/update/delete applications.
- Authorized Connect Apps
  - List/fetch authorized connect apps.
- Available Phone Numbers
  - Country-level listing and specific types: local, machine-to-machine, mobile, national, shared-cost, toll-free, VoIP; fetch country details.
- Balance
  - Fetch account balance (changes may not be immediate; child accounts do not contain balance info).
- Calls
  - List/create/fetch/update/delete calls.
  - Update can redirect an in-progress call or terminate it.
  - Delete removes the call record from API and portal logs.
  - Events: list all events for a call.
  - Notifications: fetch/list call notifications.
  - Recordings (per-call): list/create/fetch/update/delete.
    - Update recording supports status changes: pause, stop, in-progress.
    - Use Twilio.CURRENT instead of a recording SID to reference the current active recording.
- Conferences
  - List/fetch/update conferences.
  - Conference recordings: list/fetch/update/delete.
    - Update supports Twilio.CURRENT for the current recording.
- Connect Apps
  - List/fetch/update/delete connect apps.
- Dependent Phone Numbers
  - List dependent phone numbers.
- Incoming Phone Numbers
  - List/create/purchase; fetch/update/delete numbers.
  - Assigned Add-ons: list/create/fetch/delete installations on a number; list/fetch extensions for an assigned add-on.
  - Number types: local, mobile, toll-free each support list/create.
- API Keys
  - Keys: list/create new key; fetch/update/delete key.
- Media (Message media)
  - List/fetch/delete media for a specific message.
- Queue Members
  - List/fetch members; update to dequeue a member and start TwiML execution at a given URL.
- Messages
  - List/create/send/fetch/update/delete messages.
  - Update is used to redact the body or cancel not-yet-sent messages.
  - Message Feedback: create feedback to confirm a tracked user action by the recipient.
- Notifications
  - List/fetch notifications.
- Outgoing Caller IDs
  - List/fetch/update/delete caller IDs.
  - Validation Requests: create a validation request for a caller ID.
- Participants (Conference participants)
  - List/create/add; fetch/update; delete to kick a participant.
- Payments (Pay Connector)
  - Create starts a new payments session; update progresses different phases of the payment flow.
- Queues
  - List/create; fetch/update; delete (remove an empty queue).
- Realtime Transcriptions
  - Create a transcription; update to stop a transcription using its SID or the name given at creation.
- Recordings (top-level)
  - List/fetch/delete recordings.
  - Add-on Results: list/fetch; delete a result to purge all associated payloads.
  - Result Payloads: list/fetch; delete payloads and associated data.
  - Result Payload Data: fetch payload data.
  - Recording Transcriptions: list/fetch/delete.
- Short Codes
  - List/fetch/update short codes.
- Signing Keys
  - List/create new signing keys; fetch/update/delete signing keys.

Notes
- Special tokens: Twilio.CURRENT can be used with recording update endpoints to target the current active recording (applies to call and conference recording updates).
- Balance for child accounts is not available.
- Message update supports redaction and cancellation before send.
- Queue member update dequeues and begins TwiML at a provided URL.
- Realtime transcription stop supports identification by SID or by name.
