Tool `OpenAPI Explorer:getApiOperation` with Parameter {'id': 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/stripe/openapi/master/openapi/spec3.json', 'operationIdOrRoute': '/v1/customers'} on OpenAPI Explorer succeeded. Result (summarized from 917177 tokens): Stripe API (OpenAPI 3.0)
- Title: Stripe API
- Version: 2025-11-17.clover
- Description: Stripe REST API (see https://stripe.com/docs/api)
- Terms: https://stripe.com/us/terms/
- Contact: Stripe Dev Platform Team, dev-platform@stripe.com, https://stripe.com

Endpoint: GET /v1/customers (operationId: GetCustomers)
- Purpose: Returns a list of your customers, sorted by creation date (newest first).

Query parameters (all optional):
- created: Filter by creation time.
  - Either a Unix timestamp integer, or a range object with any of: gt, gte, lt, lte (integers).
- email: Case-sensitive filter on the customer’s email (string).
- limit: Number of objects to return (1–100, default 10).
- starting_after: Pagination cursor (object ID) to fetch the next page after the given ID.
- ending_before: Pagination cursor (object ID) to fetch the previous page before the given ID.
- expand: Array of response fields to expand.
- test_clock: Only include customers associated with the specified test clock. If not set, customers with test clocks are excluded.

Request body:
- application/x-www-form-urlencoded: No fields (optional; not used for GET).

Response (200, application/json):
- A list object containing:
  - data: Array of Customer objects.

Customer object (key fields):
- address (nullable): Postal address
  - city
  - country (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2)
  - line1
  - line2
  - postal_code
  - state
- balance (integer): Current balance in the customer’s default currency.
  - Negative: credit to apply to next invoice.
  - Positive: amount owed to add to next invoice.
  - Only includes amounts not yet applied to any invoice; doesn’t reflect unpaid invoices.
  - Considered only after invoices finalize.
  - For multi-currency balances, see invoice_credit_balance.
- business_name (string): Customer’s business name.
- cash_balance (nullable): Customer cash balance (represents real funds)
  - available (map[currency] -> amount in smallest currency unit); cannot delete a customer with any cash balances (even 0).
  - customer: ID of the customer this balance belongs to.
  - livemode: true for live mode, false for test mode.
  - object: "cash_balance".
  - settings:
    - reconciliation_mode: "automatic" | "manual" (how funds are reconciled to PaymentIntents using source=cash_balance).
    - using_merchant_default: boolean indicating if using account default vs customer-specific setting.
  - Use: funds can be added via bank transfer, used for payments, and eventually paid out.
- created (integer, unix time seconds): Creation timestamp.
- currency (nullable, ISO 3-letter): Default currency for recurring billing.
- default_source: The default payment source for the customer:
  - Either a string ID or a bank account object (customer bank accounts are payment methods on Customer objects; distinct from external accounts on connected Accounts).

Behavior highlights:
- Sorting: List results are ordered by created descending (most recent first).
- Pagination: Use starting_after and ending_before with object IDs returned by the API to page forward/backward.
- Expansion: Use expand[] to include nested objects inline.
- Test clocks: Pass test_clock to include only customers tied to that test clock; otherwise such customers are omitted.

Notes:
- All currency amounts are in the smallest currency unit where specified.
- Many string fields in the spec include max lengths; functionally, they are standard strings for filtering or display.
