Endpoint: GET /v1/checkout/sessions
- OperationId: GetCheckoutSessions
- Description: Returns a list of Checkout Sessions.

Query parameters (all optional)
- created: Filter by creation time.
  - Either an integer (Unix timestamp) or an object with range operators:
    - gt, gte, lt, lte (integers)
- customer: string (Customer ID). Only sessions for this Customer.
- customer_details (deepObject):
  - email: string. Only sessions matching this email in customer details.
- ending_before: string. Backward pagination cursor (object ID from a previous page).
- expand: array of strings. Fields to expand in the response.
- limit: integer. 1–100 (default 10).
- payment_intent: string (PaymentIntent ID). Only sessions for this PaymentIntent.
- payment_link: string (Payment Link ID). Only sessions for this Payment Link.
- starting_after: string. Forward pagination cursor (object ID).
- status: string enum: complete | expired | open. Only sessions with this status.
- subscription: string (Subscription ID). Only sessions for this Subscription.

Request body
- Optional; content type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded; schema has no properties (effectively unused for GET).

Response
- 200 OK, application/json
- Schema includes:
  - data: array of Checkout Session objects.

Checkout Session (key concepts and notable fields)
- Purpose: Represents a customer’s session to pay for one-time purchases or subscriptions via Stripe Checkout or Payment Links. Create a new session for each payment attempt. After successful payment, the session references the Customer and either a PaymentIntent or an active Subscription. You can create a session server-side and redirect to its URL to start Checkout. Related guide: https://stripe.com/docs/checkout/quickstart
- Fields (selected):
  - adaptive_pricing (nullable): Settings for price localization with Adaptive Pricing.
    - enabled (boolean): Whether Adaptive Pricing is available on eligible sessions.
  - after_expiration (nullable): Configuration for actions if the session expires.
    - recovery (nullable):
      - enabled (boolean): If true, generates a recovery URL when the session expires.
      - allow_promotion_codes (boolean): Enables user-redeemable promotion codes on recovered sessions (default false).
      - expires_at (integer, unix-time, nullable): Recovery URL expiration time.
      - url (string, nullable): URL that creates a new session copying the expired one.
  - allow_promotion_codes (boolean, nullable): Enables user-redeemable promotion codes.
  - amount_subtotal (integer, nullable): Total before discounts and taxes.
  - amount_total (integer, nullable): Total after discounts and taxes.
  - automatic_tax:
    - enabled (boolean): Whether automatic tax is enabled for the session.
    - liability (optional): Party responsible for tax liability; may be an account ID (string) or an Account object.

Notes
- Pagination uses starting_after and ending_before cursors.
- expand lets you request expanded sub-resources.
- Filtering supports creation time ranges, customer/customer email, payment intent/link, status, and subscription.
